yboy Club the club's bunnies featured  future stars Amber Heard Jenna Dewan and  Laura Benanti gonna be the first  chocolate centerfold I am you can't  discriminate against these babies the  Playboy Club felt some backlash with the  Parents Television Council calling the  show degrading and sexualizing and  asking audiences to boycott their  request was backed up by activist Gloria  Steinem who said the show portrayed the  tackiest place on earth as glamorous  although many blamed the  behind-the-scenes drama for the show's  bad buzz some insiders offered other  reasons for the show's failure to  connect with audiences one source said  it was a fundamentally flawed concept  it's a soap which inherently appeals to  women but it's a brand so tied to men I  just think it was doomed from the start  the series brought in only five million  viewers in its premiere falling to 3.8  million and 3.2 million for its final  two episodes we are men the quick demise  of CBS's we are men proves that  sometimes even big stars aren't enough  to save a show the comedy series brought  together Tony Shalhoub kalpen and Jerry  O'Connell along with Rob Greenberg but  their collective star power couldn't  prevent the show from getting the axe  after two episodes dad you know Fiona's  mama told ago outfit well let's go to  lunch great she's super nice in his  really big boobs organ er we are men  premiered to 6.4 million viewers  dropping to 5.4 million viewers for its  second episode the show failed to hold  on to the audience of its lead in How I  Met Your Mother and it's performance  made it a disappointing precursor to  CBS's other big comedy to bro  girls the network determined that reruns  of the Big Bang Theory and eventually  Mike and Molly would fare better in the  slot wicked city the ed Westwick led  drama wicked city was set in 1982 Los  Angeles and followed two police  detectives on a mission to capture the  notorious Hollywood Slayer and it lasted  only three episodes are you